[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Its reports said otherwise.
Read by body and placed by tenant, they hold three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October
with two outcomes. The third problem is still open.

<Callout>
Two problems closed on 5 October: `parser` fixed, `hint` won't fix. `one-day-move` is still open. The counts below are the desk's own view,
computed from the reports at render time, so they move when the desk merges more.
</Callout>

## The problems

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | counted in the table as | outcome | tracked in |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the `parser` row | fixed 5 Oct: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | [issue #1](https://github.com/daniel-packard/what-it-shows/issues/1), closed |
| `hint` | the `hint` row | won't fix 5 Oct: booking-v3 form retired | [issue #2](https://github.com/daniel-packard/what-it-shows/issues/2), closed |
| `one-day-move` | the one-day-move note: filed under `parser` by tenant, so also inside the `parser` row | **open**: not covered by the 5 Oct update | [issue #3](https://github.com/daniel-packard/what-it-shows/issues/3), open |

### `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

Day-first tenants write `07/04`, the parser reads 4 July. The day and month swap. This is the bug
#4471 was opened for, and most of its reports. **Fixed 5 October.**

### `hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, and the form
reads it the tenant's way, day first. **Won't fix: booking-v3 was retired 5 October**, so no new
reports of this kind can arrive. Only reports sent through the booking-v3 form, from day-first
tenants. The parser fix does not touch it: the form needs its hint changed. Intake tags miss it both
ways, so place these reports by tenant and channel, not by tag.

### `one-day-move`: dates off by exactly one day

A flipped day and month cannot move a date by one day. These reports describe something else: the
same meeting on Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto, every June booking a day off, an invite
that arrived before its booking. That points at time zones or daylight saving, not at date order. **Still open:** the dd/mm fix does
not touch it, and closing #4471 did not close it.
The desk read them this way already. They stay counted where they are
filed, under `parser`, and are tracked on their own.

## How to place a new report

1. Read the body. A date off by one day is `one-day-move`; add its id to `desk-notes.json`.
2. Otherwise look up the tenant: reports through the booking-v3 form are `hint`.
3. Everything else from a day-first tenant is `parser`.

Do not merge on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)): all
three problems arrive under the same subjects.

